# Intro
A star lights an upstream molecular slab at rest, then a molecular cloud that moves along
x relative to the slab. Light that crosses gas moving by more than three line widths
(`3 b`, `b = sqrt(2 k T / m_H2)`, 0.64 km/s at 50 K) relative to the column it carries sees
fresh absorption: the transport resets the carried column. The check reads particles
inside the cloud and compares their line transmission with the column of the cloud alone
(reset) or with slab plus cloud (no reset). Read the README of `ISRFH2StarLit` for the build,
the table, the parameters that the run holds fixed and the exit classes.

# Run
```
./run.sh                       # cloud at 10 widths: expect the reset
widths=1 run_name=control ./run.sh   # cloud at 1 width: expect no reset
```
`makeIC.py --widths` sets the relative speed in units of `b`. The check picks the expected
case from the speed written in `fixture.json`: more than 3 widths gives the reset.

# Checking
Per particle in the cloud at `r < L/2 - 2h`, `|ln(ratio / f)| <= s l_hop / d`, with `f` the
shielding function at the expected column and `d` the path inside the cloud. The speed of
1 width is the control: a run that shows a reset there fails.
